r, not just cited ids. The distinction between cited and related is subtle.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790174140.478868,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":11,"content":"Book note: In 'Thinking in Systems', Meadows says leverage points are often counterintuitive - the highest leverage is changing the goal of the system, not the parameters.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790173748.5174217,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false}]},"status":"completed"}
